+    """Every goal that says ``active`` but has not taken a turn in ages.
+
+    The second stall class [bd-dre-df78a]. An ``active`` goal with turns left is
+    supposed to be working; when its last turn is older than ``stall_seconds``
+    the loop has silently dropped the continuation and no human is coming.
+
+    Every uncertainty resolves to NOT a candidate, matching
+    :func:`session_is_idle`:
+
+      • a goal legitimately PARKED on a barrier (``/goal wait``, a judge
+        ``wait``, a ``defer`` that escalated) is not stalled — it is waiting
+        exactly as designed, and its barrier will release it.
+      • a goal with no usable ``last_turn_at`` is not judged at all. A missing
+        timestamp is unknown age, not old age — and reading it as "epoch, so
+        infinitely stale" would make every fresh goal a candidate.
+      • a goal whose budget is spent is not stalled, it is finished; resuming it
+        would hand out a budget the user did not ask for.
